      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "France 24 reports that Musk is among more than 150,000 people calling for Jensen Huang to return to Nvidia.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:c7c573833cdd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "U.S. Attorney General Todd Blanche said on November 12 that the Justice Department has not yet reached a conclusion on whether Alice Huang was acting as a spy for Beijing.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386110886:94"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Jen-Hsun \"Jensen\" Huang, born February 17, 1963, is a Taiwanese and American electrical engineer and businessman.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386110886:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Jensen Huang was born on 17 February 1963 in Taipei.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P569",
        "wd:Q305177:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Records show he was educated at Stanford University, Aloha High School, Oneida Baptist Institute and 2 more.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q41506",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q4734192",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q7093656",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q7375693",
        "wd:Q305177:P69:Q861888"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "He is recorded as having worked in Los Altos.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P937:Q864124"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "Wikidata lists 6 awards, among them the Queen Elizabeth Prize for Engineering (2025) and the National Medal of Science (2026).",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q305177:P166:Q4273323",
        "wd:Q305177:P166:Q737051"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:57Z",
      "text": "The Guardian headlined it: “Elon Musk joins 165,000 others calling for Nvidia to bring back Jensen Huang in open letter”",
      "cites": [
        "news:guardian:35e3e8b4f8d8"
